# version.rules — yamlmuster ruleset for the SPAR spec-version gate.
# Wired in Wave 2c. Translated from spar-validate.tcl validate_spec_version;
# loaded by spar::_yamlmuster_version and driven by that proc.
#
# BOTH rules are PREDICATES, not oneof/require. Reason (task rule: a legacy
# message that interpolates something the template vocabulary cannot express
# belongs to a predicate): each message interpolates the per-call $label
# ("campaign.yaml" or "segment '<x>'") and $CURRENT_SPEC_VERSION, neither of
# which is a node field or a template token. design-muster assigned these to
# oneof (version_unsupported) + require (version_unstamped); that is not
# viable for message fidelity, and it leaves the `oneof` kind with no
# surviving user. See DRAFT-NOTES d.
#
# Call shape (design-migration Wave 2c): the facts arrive via -context, so
# the data argument is a throwaway root dict (may be {}):
#   validate {} -groups {version} -context {declared <declared> label <label>}
# The wrapper (validate_spec_version) stays thin around this; CURRENT_SPEC_
# VERSION is the host constant the predicates read (spar::CURRENT_SPEC_VERSION).

level root -keys {}

# version_unstamped: legacy 766-770. Warning, emitted when declared eq "".
# Predicate reads context.declared / context.label and builds:
#   "<label> has no version: field — treating as pre-<CURRENT> (unstamped). Stamp it with version: \"<CURRENT>\"."
rule predicate root version_unstamped -severity warning -needs {declared label} \
    -code version_unstamped \
    -message {campaign/segment has no version: field (unstamped)} \
    -groups {version}

# version_unsupported: legacy 771-775. Error, emitted when declared is
# non-empty and != CURRENT_SPEC_VERSION (predicate guards declared ne ""
# first so the two are mutually exclusive, as in legacy). Builds:
#   "<label> declares spec version '<declared>' but this tool supports <CURRENT>."
rule predicate root version_unsupported -severity error -needs {declared label} \
    -code version_unsupported \
    -message {declared spec version is not supported by this tool} \
    -groups {version}
